    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class in the project, and it passes. The full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nOn a successful owner create, a welcome notification is now enqueued via the `NOTIFY` logger carrying the owner id and memberId.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New step function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`: reads the created `Owner` via `@Val` and emits `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId())`. It mirrors the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` pattern (dedicated named logger, runs after save so the id is populated).\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `evaluateBulkSignupWarning`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` test passes \u2014 the captured `NOTIFY` line (`welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`) contains both the owner id and the memberId \u2014 and `mvn test` reports BUILD SUCCESS with no failures.",
